[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2889062293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106529#issuecomment-2889062293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106529","id":2889062293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sM5eV","user":{"login":"tancop","id":40056096,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDU2MDk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40056096?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop","html_url":"https://github.com/tancop","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tancop/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-18T15:43:18Z","updated_at":"2025-05-18T15:43:18Z","body":"Tested this with the placeholder export option in Blender and it works without leaks. Looks like the problem is the way Godot imports materials or Blender exports them not with uv maps","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2889062293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3059691465","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106529#issuecomment-3059691465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106529","id":3059691465,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62Xy_J","user":{"login":"hilloftheking","id":91853499,"node_id":"U_kgDOBXmSuw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91853499?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking","html_url":"https://github.com/hilloftheking","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hilloftheking/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T00:27:56Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T00:27:56Z","body":"This is because materials exported from Blender have backface culling disabled by default, which seems to heavily affect light bleeding. In Blender 4.4.3, you have to enable camera backface culling in your material properties for it to be exported with backface culling.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3059691465/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5619806753","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106529#issuecomment-5619806753","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106529","id":5619806753,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTvdyIQ","user":{"login":"tinomarques","id":59707674,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NzA3Njc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59707674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques","html_url":"https://github.com/tinomarques","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:53:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T13:54:40Z","body":"Also came across this issue in my project, and the following fixed it:\n\nIn `scene/3d/lightmap_gi.cpp` line 1190, the lightmapper reads the original mesh material when collecting material information for ray tracing. It ignores the overrides stored in `mf.overrides`, although those overrides are used when rendering the material for the bake.\n\nThis change makes that lookup use the override when available:\n```diff\n- Ref<Material> mat = mf.mesh->surface_get_material(i);\n+ Ref<Material> mat = i < mf.overrides.size() && mf.overrides[i].is_valid() ? mf.overrides[i] : mf.mesh->surface_get_material(i);\n```\n\nHaven't checked if it resolves all cases reported here, but hopefully can be of help!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5619806753/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]